course: dictionary
lesson: 9007
title: Skills you can build
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A skill is something you can do well because you have learned it and practised it. Skill is the ability to do something well. Nobody is born able to ride a bike or read well: they build the skill over time.
explain: Look at the words around skill to find its meaning. «Sleep is the part of training where the body does its building, and the brain stores the new skills.» Stores and building tell you that skills are things the brain keeps and grows, not things you find by luck.
explain: You can be good at one skill and still be learning another. «Neat letters and good writing are different skills: a brilliant story can come in messy letters.» When you want to improve, ask yourself: what could I practise to get better?
fact: A skill is something you can do well because you have learned and practised it.
fact: Skill means the ability to do something well.
fact: Skills include reading, counting, dribbling, catching, swimming, cooking and drawing.
fact: «Learning your address by heart is a real safety skill.»
fact: «Switching between styles is a skill, not being fake.» Skills can be learned, so practice helps.
exercise: «Practice builds skills.» What is a skill? | Something you were born knowing without trying | *Something you can do well because you have learned and practised it | A tool for cutting wood | A prize you win in a race
exercise: Which of these is a safety skill? | Drawing a cat | Eating crisps in bed | Singing very loudly | *Crossing the road safely
exercise: Which of these is a sport skill? | *Catching a ball | Writing a shopping list | Sleeping late | Losing your school bag
test: Is a skill something you are born knowing? | Yes, every skill comes at birth | Yes, but only in sport | Only if you are a prodigy | *No, you learn it and practise it
test: Which word is the plural of skill? | *skills | skilful | skill | skilles
exam: In «Switching between styles is a skill, not being fake», what does skill mean? | A rule you must obey | *Something you can do well because you have learned and practised it | Something you are born knowing | Being fake
